---
import BlogHeader from "@/components/blog/BlogHeader.astro";
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";

// Keep the wording in sync with OrbitHop Docs/site/privacy.html.
const site = Astro.site ?? new URL("https://avanegas.com");
const canonicalUrl = new URL("/privacy/", site).href;
const email = "avanegas95@gmail.com";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy: Astro Andy: Orbit Hop"
  description="Privacy policy for Astro Andy: Orbit Hop, a one-tap arcade game for iPhone."
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
>
  <BlogHeader active="none" />
  <main
    class="pt-[calc(var(--nav-height)+2rem)] pb-16 max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6"
  >
    <header class="mb-10 fade-in">
      <p class="text-[var(--sec)] font-mono text-sm mb-2">
        Astro Andy: Orbit Hop
      </p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--white)] mb-4">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-[var(--white-icon)] leading-relaxed">
        Last updated 1 October 2026
      </p>
    </header>

    <article class="blog-prose fade-in">
      <p>
        Astro Andy: Orbit Hop ("the game") is a one-tap arcade game for iPhone.
        This page explains what data the game uses and who handles it. The short
        version: <strong
          >there are no accounts, we run no servers, and we never receive your
          personal information.</strong
        > The only outside service that collects data is Google AdMob, and only if
        you choose to watch an optional rewarded ad.
      </p>

      <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
      <p>
        Your scores, Stardust, unlocked pilots and trails, settings and daily
        streak are stored on your iPhone. They are never sent to us.
      </p>

      <h2>iCloud sync</h2>
      <p>
        If you are signed in to iCloud, the game copies the same progress to
        your own iCloud account (iCloud key-value storage) so it follows you to
        your other devices. This data lives in your Apple account; we cannot see
        or access it. You can turn this off in the iOS Settings app under your
        name &gt; iCloud.
      </p>

      <h2>Game Center</h2>
      <p>
        If you are signed in to Game Center, the game sends your scores and
        achievements to Apple's Game Center so they appear on the leaderboard
        and in your profile. Apple handles this under its <a
          href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">privacy policy</a
        >; we never see or store your Game Center ID.
      </p>

      <h2>Ads (Google AdMob)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The game shows only <strong
            >rewarded ads that you choose to watch</strong
          > ("Double it" after a run). There are no banner ads and no forced ads.
        </li>
        <li>
          Ads are provided by Google AdMob. We request <strong
            >non-personalized ads</strong
          > and we do not use Apple's App Tracking Transparency prompt or your device's
          advertising identifier (IDFA).
        </li>
        <li>
          To serve and measure ads and to prevent fraud, Google may process
          information such as your device's IP address (used for approximate
          location), device and app information, and how you interact with the
          ad. This data is handled by Google under the <a
            href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Privacy Policy</a
          > and
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
            >how Google uses information from sites or apps that use its
            services</a
          >. We do not receive it in a form that identifies you.
        </li>
        <li>
          The Google Mobile Ads SDK may also collect crash and performance
          diagnostics about the ad code.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="consent" class="scroll-mt-[calc(var(--nav-height)+1rem)]">
        Consent (EEA, UK and Switzerland)
      </h2>
      <p>
        Where the law requires it, the game shows Google's consent form (User
        Messaging Platform) the first time an ad is about to be offered, never
        at launch. If consent is not given, no ads are requested. Supporter Pack
        owners never see ads.
      </p>

      <h2>In-app purchases</h2>
      <p>
        Purchases (such as the Supporter Pack) are handled
        entirely by Apple through the App Store. We do not receive your payment
        details, name or email. The game checks your purchases on your device
        with Apple's StoreKit so it can unlock what you bought and restore it on
        your other devices.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No accounts, sign-in, email or contacts.</li>
        <li>
          No analytics or tracking tools of our own, and no servers of our own.
        </li>
        <li>No precise location, camera, microphone, photos or health data.</li>
        <li>We do not sell your data.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        The game is suitable for all ages and is not directed specifically at
        children. Ads are non-personalized. We do not knowingly collect personal
        information from anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Simply don't tap "Double it": no ad is loaded or shown unless an offer
          is made, and none plays unless you tap it.
        </li>
        <li>
          Change your ad consent choice from "Privacy choices" in the game's
          Settings (shown where the law requires consent).
        </li>
        <li>
          Delete the app to remove all data stored on the device; remove the
          iCloud copy from iOS Settings &gt; your name &gt; iCloud &gt; Manage
          Storage.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page
        with a new date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about privacy: <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</Layout>
